Context: comparative discovery; Product Alpha Q3 portfolio anchors retained
Interview date: 2026-07-13

Q: What do you check before trusting an exported report?
A: B-02 compares the visible count to the downloaded rows and looks for the
time range. They said, "A download is not proof that I exported the right
thing." Missing filters create a second manual review before a leadership
handoff.

Q: What would reduce that review?
A: A stable export summary with query scope, row count, generation timestamp,
and omitted fields. If a permission excludes records, the export should say so
without exposing the records themselves.

Q: Is automation useful here?
A: A scheduled weekly export is useful only after the first manual export has
been verified. B-02 wanted the schedule owner and recipient group visible,
plus a preview that can be cancelled before delivery.

Initial codes: export confidence; admin automation; time-to-first-value.
Researcher note: The participant described auditability of a handoff, not a
request for unrestricted data access.
